    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of two numbers, we can use prime factorization. First, let's find the prime factorization of each number:\n\nPrime factorization of 40:\n\\[ 40 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 5 \\]\n\\[ 40 = 2^3 \\times 5^1 \\]\n\nPrime factorization of 48:\n\\[ 48 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 \\]\n\\[ 48 = 2^4 \\times 3^1 \\]\n\nThe GCF is found by taking the lowest power of each prime factor that appears in both factorizations. Here, the only prime factor common to both 40 and 48 is 2, and the lowest power of 2 that appears in both factorizations is \\(2^3\\).\n\nTherefore, the GCF of 40 and 48 is \\(2^3 = 8\\). \n\nFinal answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
